From f89d678c9cc5f11941eff32cab3caee21eac3e7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Forever Twins research)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:09:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Forever Twins: G1 and G2 helper templates, tested on 11 real
 sources

Summary
- templates/forever-twin-helper-v2.clar.tmpl now renders two groups:
  G1 (plain owner transfer) = unchanged base helper;
  G2 (source has its own listing market) = base + fail-closed listing guard
  (swap-original-for-twin refuses with u217 unless the source reports no
  listing before and after the deposit; is-source-listed read-only added).
- render-helper.mjs: new config fields group and listingReadFn; render-all.mjs
  renders every simnet instance; rendered mainnet examples for review
  (zombie-wabbits.G1, megapont-ape-club.G2).
- prepare-legacy.mjs + legacy-sources.json: archived sources prepared for
  simnet with only [simnet]-marked trait lines changed (test mint appended
  only where the real mint needs live sale state).
- sim/family-suite.mjs: same checks on Zombie Wabbits, Citadels, Funky Donuts,
  Blocks (G1) and Bitcoin Pepe, The Guests, Bitslimes, Leo Cats, Tigress,
  Megapont Ape Club, Satoshibles (G2), plus mock-leaky-market proving the G1
  helper would be drained where G2 refuses.

Verification
- npm test: 428/428 (existing 60, acceptance 70, families 278, probes 8,
  live-check 12). Simnet only; mainnet-fork runs still required.

Notes
- Templates remain unaudited prototypes; nothing here authorises deployment.
